        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185269030?u=1fc22565ccf4566b6f734fabaa87e03d9a31cfe4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #30932.\">Closes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5955222774\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30932\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30932/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30932\">#30932</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari supports <code class=\"notranslate\">datalist</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;input type=\"range\"&gt;</code> since 12.1, but tick marks and option labels disappear when:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">appearance: none</code> is applied to the range input</li>\n<li>the <code class=\"notranslate\">datalist</code> is given a visible <code class=\"notranslate\">display</code> value</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31063",
            "title": "fix(html): add Safari notes for datalist with styled range inputs",
            "date_modified": "2026-11-06T19:52:01.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-11-05T12:41:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "BHUVANSH855",
                "url": "https://github.com/BHUVANSH855"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.21.1) found new features shipping in Safari Technical Preview 255 on macOS 27 which was released yesterday. Currently, the collector covers about 90% of BCD, so the following list might not be exhaustive.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Release notes: <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/18602/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-256/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/18602/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-256/</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updated keys:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>api.CanvasRenderingContext2D.fontKerning</li>\n<li>api.CanvasRenderingContext2D.fontStretch</li>\n<li>api.CanvasRenderingContext2D.fontVariantCaps</li>\n<li>api.CanvasRenderingContext2D.lang</li>\n<li>api.CanvasRenderingContext2D.textRendering</li>\n<li>api.OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D.fontKerning</li>\n<li>api.OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D.fontStretch</li>\n<li>api.OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D.fontVariantCaps</li>\n<li>api.OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D.lang</li>\n<li>api.OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D.textRendering</li>\n<li>api.SVGAElement.referrerPolicy</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Notes:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>I have another open PR for Safari TP 255: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"6165994087\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/31024\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31024/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31024\">#31024</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31058",
            "title": "Updates for Safari TP 256",
            "date_modified": "2026-11-05T10:10:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-11-05T10:08:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.21.1) found new features shipping in Safari 27.1 on iPhone Duo which was released last week.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is just about Device Posture API and Viewport Segment API. Both behind a flag. See <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/18486/webkit-features-for-safari-27-1/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/18486/webkit-features-for-safari-27-1/</a></p>",
