            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR replaces <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5628048996\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30697\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30697/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30697\">#30697</a>. I've recreated it to use a ranged statement to indicate that there was full support between 126-156. It is partial from 156 onwards and will likely be removed completely in the future.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Original PR comment:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/c9w5uH3eSuo/m/oG9HX5UfCQAJ\" rel=\"nofollow\">This message from intent to remove sent on Sept 28:</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We landed the required code in M156. The fenced frame element and window.fence are now stubs starting in M156. We will start the experiment to remove the stubs in M157. Thanks!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6366274495053824\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chrome Status entry (updated recently)</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This Chromium commit removed Fenced Frames API:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8144621\" rel=\"nofollow\">CL 8144621</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/55fa5f273aed691fbe11a449cabf1943fb284f74\">This commit on GitHub</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/fenced-frame/fenced-frame-stub.https.html\">WPT test for stubs</a> - this explains all the <code class=\"notranslate\">notes</code> I added.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a direct follow-up to my earlier PR deprecating Fenced Frame API <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5161427314\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30242\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30242/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30242\">#30242</a><br>\nThis is relaed to Shared Storeage API PR I created <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5568937249\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30659\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30659/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30659\">#30659</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31038",
            "title": "[Google Privacy Sandbox] Chrome 156 stubs out Fenced Frame API",
            "date_modified": "2026-11-03T12:07:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-11-03T12:06:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.21.1) found new features shipping in today's Chromium Canary.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">HTML install element, <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152834368700416\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152834368700416</a> (says 158, but I couldn't confirm this)</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>api.HTMLInstallElement</li>\n<li>api.HTMLInstallElement.invalidReason</li>\n<li>api.HTMLInstallElement.isValid</li>\n<li>api.HTMLInstallElement.manifest</li>\n<li>api.HTMLInstallElement.manifestId</li>\n<li>api.HTMLInstallElement.validationstatuschange_event</li>\n<li>api.InstallResultEvent</li>\n<li>api.InstallResultEvent.InstallResultEvent</li>\n<li>api.InstallResultEvent.result</li>\n<li>api.Navigator.install</li>\n<li>html.elements.install</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Webtransport exportKeyingMaterial, <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/4860330806214656\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/4860330806214656</a> (also says 158, but I couldn't confirm this either)</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>api.WebTransport.exportKeyingMaterial</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31026",
